{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>Wisdom.</b> Because he said, 'Do not be overly wise,' he returned to explain that there is no greatness greater than it; rather, he warned not to engage in it constantly but to give a portion to the body so that it may live. And he said: for wisdom has more might and power than the might of many rulers. And why ten? Because it is the sum of counting and is the head of the whole, for all that is beyond it are ones. And because the essence of every thing is its head, its middle, and its end, therefore in the holy tongue the alef was at the beginning and the yod at the end, and the heh and vav were in the middle. And these four letters are for drawing out, and it is impossible to find a letter or a vowel except that one of them is drawn along with it. And the alef and yod in calculation guard themselves like a wall, and the heh and vav are circular calculation, and a great sod is in all of them in the honored and awesome Name that is not a name of measure, and it is composed of the aforementioned letters. And the matter of 'were in the city' is to show their might when all of them are joined in one place in one accord. And some interpret that this alludes to the spheres, and he added one, and it is not correct."], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {0 "The phrase 'והוסיף אחד' is obscure; translated hyper-literally as 'and he added one.' It may refer to an interpreter who adds an eleventh element to the ten, but the referent is uncertain."}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:28:14.714709189Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}